-- Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames, Lord Kreelo's power armor and three war vehicles (printed 116-124)
-- 4 vehicle rows, with 36 locations and 19 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~344-megaverse-in-flames-kreelo-arms.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.
--
-- The power armor is a vehicles row and the two body armors are gear (ruling of
-- 2026-11-17; not taken: all three as gear). Every M.D.C. by Location block,
-- damage, cost and P.P.E. figure was read off a render of its page.
-- A WEAPON PRINTED INSIDE A VEHICLE is that vehicle's weapon entry only: none of
-- them (the Chaos Trooper's Lightning Forearm Gun, the Lightning Cannons) prints
-- a price of its own, so none is a gear row. Every numbered weapon system is
-- stored, the non-weapon ones (troops, riders, spell casting) with no damage.
-- FIGURES THE BOOK PRINTS TWO WAYS, stored as printed and noted in the row: the
-- Carnage Tank carries four large demons in its Crew line and six in its Cargo
-- line; the Walking Death's side cannons are "(2, each side)" at 100 M.D.C. each,
-- four in all as weapon system 2 counts them. The Chaos Trooper's weapon 1 is
-- headed Lightning Forearm Gun and called the Lightning Cannon in its text.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('bew-chaos-trooper-armor', 'BEW Chaos Trooper Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One', NULL, 'Running 30 mph (48 km), or the wearer''s own speed +20% if that is faster; adds 30 ft (9.1 m) to leaps', 'Adds 100 mph (160 km) to the wearer''s flying speed, and can hover; a wearer who cannot fly gets 100 mph (160 km) at most. Thrusters run 10 hours, then must cool or they shut down', 'None; the thrusters fail underwater', 'Adds 20% to the wearer''s height and 10% to his width; weight 1,000 lbs (450 kg)', '0.5', 200, 1, NULL, 2300000, '2.3 million credits for a 5-10 ft (1.5-3 m) suit; 4.5 million for one under 22 ft (6.7 m); 6 million for one up to 32 ft (9.7 m). Every size has the same stats.', 'Hellspawn-200, a Chaos Armor Military Assault Suit from Lord Kreelo''s Megaverse Armaments. A magical power armor sold to demons (a more technological look) and Deevils (spiky and medieval), built for big supernatural frames such as Gallu, Gargoyles, Baal-Rogs, Dragons, Deevils, Beasts and Horrors. It is only half a suit with thin plating, so the wearer can still work magic, and it leaves openings for wings, with a thruster over each shoulder. Sensors: crude radar to 5 miles (8 km), tracking 48 targets; +1 to long-range attacks. Power: Soulmancy, fed by the wearer: 10 P.P.E. and 20 M.D.C. run the suit for two hours, and Bio-Regeneration stops while it is worn until it is removed or idle for an hour. Soulmancy enhancements, each paid in the wearer''s M.D.C., which then will not Bio-Regenerate until the suit comes off or he rests an hour, and then only at half rate: Blood Spray (as the Soulmancy spell, 6th level, 2 M.D.C. a use); Strength Enhancement (+5 P.S. for 10 minutes, 10 M.D.C.); Resistance Enhancement (+1 to all saving throws for 10 minutes, 15 M.D.C.). Cargo: none.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.116-118'),
  ('bew-meat-grinder-tank', 'BEW Meat Grinder Tank', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Five: driver, cab/forward passenger and three gunners', '12-14 demons in the cargo bay, more if small', '90 mph (144 km) maximum, usually cruising at 45 mph (72 km); 20 mph (32 km) or less when ploughing through infantry, wire and light fortifications. Range 500 miles (800 km) per barrel of blood', NULL, NULL, 'Height 18 ft (5.5 m); width 16 ft (4.9 m); length 38 ft (11.6 m)', '12', 560, 1, NULL, 3800000, '3.8 million credits.', 'Hellspawn-S10, a Demonic Utility Vehicle and Troop Transport from Lord Kreelo''s Megaverse Armaments; a favourite of the demons of Hades. A troop-crushing utility truck: up front two spiked rollers, one above the other, chew up anyone they catch, and a huge rolling-pin wheel behind them finishes the job; treads drive the rear. The rollers can lift 7 ft (2.1 m) to clear rocks and debris. Clawed fingers under the hull scoop up blood and pulp for Blood Pools, rituals or the fuel barrels in back. The cab, the three gun positions and the pickup-style cargo bed are open. Cargo: 28 tons, or 12-14 large demons on their feet. Power: a Soulmancy engine burning fresh blood, which it collects as it goes. Losing one rear tread halves speed and costs -25% to piloting; losing both cuts speed by 90%, though the front rollers can still drag it; losing the big wheel and both treads stops it. Troops in the cargo bay may fire over the sides or dismount, and more cargo can be lashed to the rib struts, exposed to fire.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.118-119'),
  ('bew-carnage-tank', 'BEW Carnage Tank', 'rifts', 'vehicle', '4: pilot, co-pilot/navigator, gunner, commander', 'In the lower section: four large demons or power armors of human size, or 8-10 human-sized troops; the statistics say six large demons or power armors', '85 mph (136 km) maximum, cruising 60 mph (96 km); 20 mph (32 km) up and down Hell Pit walls, cliffs and buildings, climbing with its chain launchers', NULL, '30 mph (48 km), driving along the sea floor', 'Height 18 ft (5.5 m); width 16 ft (4.9 m); length 46 ft (14 m)', '50', 700, 1, NULL, 45000000, '45 million credits each from Kreelo.', 'Hellspawn-400, a Heavy Tank from Lord Kreelo''s Megaverse Armaments, sold to both sides of the Minion War in different livery so neither knows the other is a customer: demon tanks wear a Baal-Rog face in crimson and bronze, Deevil tanks a Horror''s face in black and purple. The front is a shark-like toothed maw with searchlight eyes that bites giant foes, grips dragons, robots and vehicles, and tears up wire and light defenses; blood it takes is drained into a small Blood Pool inside, and slaves sometimes feed it corpses. Spiked treads let it cling to any surface. Range: unlimited while fed; a 20 gallon (75.7 liter) blood barrel gives 500 miles (800 km), one soul a week of running. Power: Soulmancy. Soulmancy enhancement, Stench of Hades: six times a day, a sulphurous cloud 30 ft (9.1 m) around the tank lasting 1D6 melee rounds, halved in strong wind; a foe failing a save vs magic of 12 takes 1D6 damage a melee and has a 1-50% chance a round of vomiting, losing initiative and two attacks and -4 to parry and dodge; everyone in it, saved or not, is -2 to strike, parry and dodge. Gas immunity, sealed suits or vehicles, or goggles and gas mask protect. Losing one tread halves speed with -25% to piloting; losing both stops it. Ram: 2D6 M.D. up to 45 mph (72 km), 4D6 M.D. above, +3D6 M.D. to anyone run over (weapon system 5).', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.119-121'),
  ('bew-walking-death', 'BEW Walking Death', 'rifts', 'robot', 'One or two large riders 10-25 ft (3-7.6 m) tall, or 3-6 human-sized riders; typically a pilot/commander, two gunners and any passengers', NULL, 'Running 45 mph (72 km) maximum; cannot leap. Runs a week per soul, two if used lightly', NULL, 'Walks the sea floor to 1,000 ft (305 m) deep; most mortal riders die below 200 ft (61 m) without power armor', 'Height 50 ft (15.2 m); width 21 ft (6.4 m); length 150 ft (45.7 m) from snout to tail tip', '60', 1300, 1, NULL, 100000000, '100 million credits new from Kreelo; 100-150 million second-hand.', 'Hellspawn-666, a Living Heavy Assault Robot from Lord Kreelo''s Megaverse Armaments, his answer to the Infernal Mastodon. A tortured, gutted and lobotomized giant dinosaur rebuilt with robot legs, a partial exoskeleton and barding-like plates into a T-Rex-headed riding beast and weapons platform; the riders sit in the Combat Saddle on its back, which carries the side guns and missiles. Deevil versions get extra head plating, horns, and a restyled saddle and finned or spiked tail. Attacks per melee: the commanding rider''s +3. Supernatural P.S. 35. Horror Factor 17. Power: Soulmancy. A soccer-ball-sized Soul Chamber studded with 60,000-100,000 credits of gems holds 3D6+2 souls, one consumed a week; with none left, or the chamber destroyed, it collapses within 1D6 minutes. A Blood Pillar inside powers its spells and Bio-Regeneration of 4D6 M.D.C. a melee round; destroy it and those are lost and speed and attacks are halved, though the cannons still fire on the riders'' blood. Getting at them means 50 M.D. to open the healing belly for human-sized intruders (80-100 M.D. for larger), 100 M.D. to free the 20-30 ton pillar and 100 M.D. more for a hole below it (otherwise another 200 to the belly), or explosives doing 300 or more from inside. Cargo: only a cage under the hind haunches for about a dozen prisoners, who may be sacrificed to recharge the cannons. Riders can fire from its back or dismount to fight.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.121-124');

